13
00:00:31,682 --> 00:00:33,093
and this function would be called

14
00:00:33,269 --> 00:00:36,282
isPowerOf2, then this function should return

15
00:00:36,330 --> 00:00:39,873
true for 8, which is 2 at the power of 3,

16
00:00:40,498 --> 00:00:43,030
but it should return false for 5, which is

17
00:00:43,367 --> 00:00:44,200
not a number

18
00:00:44,970 --> 00:00:47,262
that can be calculated with 2 at the power

19
00:00:47,470 --> 00:00:48,079
of something.

20
00:00:48,928 --> 00:00:52,455
So our algorithm needs to make sure that we

21
00:00:52,583 --> 00:00:55,053
produce that result. And therefore we could

22
00:00:55,069 --> 00:00:56,771
say we write an algorithm

23
00:00:57,333 --> 00:00:58,810
that does one core thing.

24
00:00:59,485 --> 00:01:01,154
It divides the input number

25
00:01:01,732 --> 00:01:02,680
8 or 5

26
00:01:03,418 --> 00:01:03,788
and all

27
00:01:04,558 --> 00:01:07,256
future division results it produces

28
00:01:07,930 --> 00:01:11,688
until 1 is reached. And then we check if the

29
00:01:11,688 --> 00:01:12,394
remainder

30
00:01:12,972 --> 00:01:14,899
is always 0.

31
00:01:15,493 --> 00:01:18,255
So if we basically were able to make that

32
00:01:18,287 --> 00:01:19,202
division by 2

33
00:01:19,796 --> 00:01:22,076
without ever producing some remainder.

34
00:01:22,381 --> 00:01:25,015
Because if we do produce a remainder, like

35
00:01:25,015 --> 00:01:27,841
when we try to divide 5 by 2, that doesn't

36
00:01:27,841 --> 00:01:29,848
work. We can't produce just an integer

37
00:01:29,848 --> 00:01:30,024
there.

38
00:01:30,570 --> 00:01:33,364
If we use the modulus operator on 5 divided

39
00:01:33,364 --> 00:01:34,536
by 2, we would get 1

40
00:01:35,211 --> 00:01:37,555
as a remainder. So if we do get a remainder,

41
00:01:37,716 --> 00:01:40,381
we know this number can't be divided by 2,

42
00:01:40,766 --> 00:01:43,030
and therefore it can't be calculated with 2

43
00:01:43,175 --> 00:01:44,556
at the power of something.

44
00:01:45,102 --> 00:01:47,189
And if we get such a remainder for any

45
00:01:47,189 --> 00:01:50,322
division then we know this will not work.

46
00:01:51,189 --> 00:01:53,359
Now this might sound very abstract, so

47
00:01:53,375 --> 00:01:54,981
therefore let's simply implement this

48
00:01:54,981 --> 00:01:57,761
together, and then I'll also show you one

49
00:01:57,809 --> 00:02:01,055
super nice smart trick with which you can

50
00:02:01,087 --> 00:02:02,356
shine in any interview.

51
00:02:03,272 --> 00:02:06,068
So here I'm again in an empty app.js file,

52
00:02:06,630 --> 00:02:09,956
and in there let's implement this isPowerOf2

53
00:02:10,326 --> 00:02:10,695
function.

54
00:02:11,290 --> 00:02:13,909
It gets a number as a parameter

55
00:02:14,808 --> 00:02:16,639
And the goal is that we can call it

56
00:02:17,233 --> 00:02:20,444
isPowerOfTwo, let's say with 8, and here we

57
00:02:20,444 --> 00:02:23,109
should get true as a result. For 5, we

58
00:02:23,109 --> 00:02:25,984
should get false. For 16, we should get

59
00:02:25,984 --> 00:02:26,256
true.

60
00:02:26,851 --> 00:02:29,131
And for, let's say, 13, we should get false.

61
00:02:29,195 --> 00:02:31,764
That's the idea. Now, how can we write this?

62
00:02:32,390 --> 00:02:35,152
I had a verbal description on the slide, but

63
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:36,902
that might have been a bit difficult to

64
00:02:36,902 --> 00:02:39,102
grasp. So let's simply implement it step by

65
00:02:39,150 --> 00:02:39,407
step.

66
00:02:40,514 --> 00:02:42,903
Well, first of all, we can check if the

67
00:02:42,903 --> 00:02:43,849
number we're getting

68
00:02:44,427 --> 00:02:47,217
is smaller than 1.

69
00:02:48,035 --> 00:02:50,617
If that's the case, we can return false

70
00:02:50,617 --> 00:02:52,686
because we know that won't work. We can't

71
00:02:52,686 --> 00:02:55,123
divide this by 2. It's certainly not

72
00:02:55,813 --> 00:02:58,154
at the power of 2. This also rules out

73
00:02:58,154 --> 00:03:00,335
negative numbers to be fed in. You could of

74
00:03:00,384 --> 00:03:02,885
course omit this if you know that you get a

75
00:03:02,885 --> 00:03:04,232
number that's at least 2

76
00:03:04,794 --> 00:03:05,435
as an input.

77
00:03:06,530 --> 00:03:08,076
So let's therefore now have a look at the

78
00:03:08,157 --> 00:03:09,394
core of this algorithm.

79
00:03:10,273 --> 00:03:12,307
For that, I'll add a new variable here,

80
00:03:14,140 --> 00:03:16,152
dividedNumber,

81
00:03:17,617 --> 00:03:19,629
and initially that's just my input number,

82
00:03:19,806 --> 00:03:21,400
but we're going to change this variable

83
00:03:21,802 --> 00:03:22,881
throughout a loop.

84
00:03:23,589 --> 00:03:25,606
And now here we could add a for loop and

85
00:03:25,671 --> 00:03:26,914
make it work with that somehow,

86
00:03:27,463 --> 00:03:29,288
but I will actually use a while loop here

87
00:03:29,805 --> 00:03:33,223
and basically check if dividedNumber is not

88
00:03:33,223 --> 00:03:33,896
equal to 1.

89
00:03:34,490 --> 00:03:36,318
And inside of the while loop, I will then

90
00:03:36,415 --> 00:03:38,885
change divided number and will gradually

91
00:03:38,981 --> 00:03:40,152
approach 1 there.

92
00:03:40,842 --> 00:03:43,088
So how will we do that? Well, we take

93
00:03:43,088 --> 00:03:43,938
divided number

94
00:03:44,676 --> 00:03:46,729
and we set this equal to divided number

95
00:03:47,002 --> 00:03:49,953
divided by 2. So we divide this number by 2,

96
00:03:50,226 --> 00:03:52,375
and we do this inside of a loop so this

97
00:03:52,375 --> 00:03:55,182
divided number gets smaller and smaller. If

98
00:03:55,199 --> 00:03:57,332
we feed in 8 to this function,

99
00:03:57,925 --> 00:04:00,059
we'll set divided number to 8 initially.

100
00:04:00,637 --> 00:04:02,562
Then we go in the while loop and we divide

101
00:04:02,562 --> 00:04:03,028
it by 2.

102
00:04:03,557 --> 00:04:06,334
So now we have 4, which is not 1, so we

103
00:04:06,334 --> 00:04:06,719
continue.

104
00:04:07,473 --> 00:04:09,961
In the next loop iteration, we divide 4 by

105
00:04:09,961 --> 00:04:12,657
2, so we have 2 in divided number then,

106
00:04:13,010 --> 00:04:14,808
which is not 1, so we continue.

107
00:04:15,498 --> 00:04:17,328
And then we go again into the loop, and

108
00:04:17,424 --> 00:04:20,489
there we had 2, we divided by 2, now we have

109
00:04:20,537 --> 00:04:23,089
1. That's our exit condition, and we're

110
00:04:23,121 --> 00:04:23,378
done.

111
00:04:24,309 --> 00:04:25,850
Now of course we'll have a problem if we

112
00:04:25,850 --> 00:04:27,198
feed in 5 though?

113
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:31,437
With 5, we have divided number equal to 5.

114
00:04:32,192 --> 00:04:34,375
We go into the loop, we divide it by 2, so

115
00:04:34,375 --> 00:04:35,821
now we have 2.5.

116
00:04:36,752 --> 00:04:40,140
And in the next iteration, we divide 2.5 by

117
00:04:40,140 --> 00:04:40,365
2,

118
00:04:40,927 --> 00:04:44,764
which is 1.25, which is not 1. So we go into

119
00:04:44,796 --> 00:04:45,679
a new iteration

120
00:04:46,305 --> 00:04:49,212
and we divide 1.25 by 2,

121
00:04:49,774 --> 00:04:52,647
which is a number smaller than 1. So this

122
00:04:52,727 --> 00:04:54,716
exit condition will not be met and we would

123
00:04:54,732 --> 00:04:57,298
have an infinite loop and we would continue

124
00:04:57,298 --> 00:04:59,607
dividing that number and we would approach

125
00:04:59,719 --> 00:05:02,718
0, therefore, we would get closer to 0 with

126
00:05:02,830 --> 00:05:03,584
every iteration.

127
00:05:04,274 --> 00:05:06,038
We would never reach 0 though

128
00:05:06,599 --> 00:05:08,459
and we therefore in the end have just an

129
00:05:08,459 --> 00:05:10,704
infinite loop because this exit condition in

130
00:05:10,704 --> 00:05:13,286
the end is never met. We never have equal to

131
00:05:13,350 --> 00:05:15,130
1, so we never would make it out of this

132
00:05:15,130 --> 00:05:15,275
loop.

133
00:05:16,237 --> 00:05:17,760
And therefore we need to add an if check

134
00:05:17,760 --> 00:05:17,953
here.

135
00:05:18,947 --> 00:05:21,096
And we need to check if divided number

136
00:05:21,754 --> 00:05:22,796
modulus 2

137
00:05:23,550 --> 00:05:26,661
is not equal to 0. And that if check simply

138
00:05:26,661 --> 00:05:29,114
makes sure that if we feed in a number that

139
00:05:29,146 --> 00:05:31,231
can't be divided by 2 anymore,

140
00:05:32,113 --> 00:05:34,246
we know about that and we have a way of

141
00:05:34,262 --> 00:05:35,192
reacting to that.

142
00:05:35,962 --> 00:05:38,271
And in there I will return false because if

143
00:05:38,271 --> 00:05:40,035
we ever make it into there, we know

144
00:05:40,596 --> 00:05:43,194
the number we fed in originally when we

145
00:05:43,194 --> 00:05:46,354
started dividing it eventually reach a point

146
00:05:46,706 --> 00:05:48,904
where we can't divide it by 2 anymore

147
00:05:49,417 --> 00:05:51,679
without creating a number that has a decimal

148
00:05:51,679 --> 00:05:54,181
place, so a non-integer number. And if

149
00:05:54,245 --> 00:05:56,619
that's the case, we know we certainly can't

150
00:05:56,619 --> 00:05:59,698
have a number that can be produced with 2 at

151
00:05:59,698 --> 00:06:02,104
the power of something. So that makes sure

152
00:06:02,104 --> 00:06:03,644
that we return false eventually.

153
00:06:04,734 --> 00:06:07,204
If we make it past this while loop, we on

154
00:06:07,237 --> 00:06:09,001
the other hand know that we have a number

155
00:06:09,001 --> 00:06:10,717
that is 2 at the power of something,

156
00:06:11,230 --> 00:06:12,914
otherwise we would have made it into the if

157
00:06:12,914 --> 00:06:14,312
check. At some point.

158
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:16,963
That's how this works.

159
00:06:18,554 --> 00:06:21,704
Now it's not enough to just generally check

160
00:06:21,785 --> 00:06:24,235
if the number that's fed in can be divided

161
00:06:24,251 --> 00:06:27,221
by 2 without producing a remainder, because

162
00:06:27,318 --> 00:06:30,643
consider the case that we feed in 20. This

163
00:06:30,643 --> 00:06:33,183
can be divided by 2, so if that would be our

164
00:06:33,458 --> 00:06:35,630
only check, if we hadn't the code down

165
00:06:35,662 --> 00:06:35,857
there,

166
00:06:36,699 --> 00:06:39,454
then we would be able to divide 20 by 2 and

167
00:06:39,471 --> 00:06:42,204
we might return false here but return true

168
00:06:42,541 --> 00:06:45,269
here therefore. So since we can divide 20 by

169
00:06:45,269 --> 00:06:47,355
2, we would not make it in there and we

170
00:06:47,372 --> 00:06:49,779
would return true. And we would indicate

171
00:06:49,779 --> 00:06:52,186
that 20 can be constructed with 2 at the

172
00:06:52,186 --> 00:06:53,085
power of something.

173
00:06:53,614 --> 00:06:56,278
But that would be wrong because 20 can be

174
00:06:56,278 --> 00:06:57,016
