175
00:06:57,867 --> 00:07:00,322
and so can the result of that division, 10.

176
00:07:01,093 --> 00:07:03,468
But the result of that division, 10 divided

177
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:06,870
by 2, which is 5, cannot be divided by 2

178
00:07:06,870 --> 00:07:09,036
anymore, at least not without producing a

179
00:07:09,052 --> 00:07:10,529
number that has a decimal place.

180
00:07:11,596 --> 00:07:14,845
So that means that whilst 20 is divisible by

181
00:07:14,894 --> 00:07:15,072
2,

182
00:07:15,702 --> 00:07:18,031
it can't be calculated with 2 at the power

183
00:07:18,111 --> 00:07:18,257
of

184
00:07:18,790 --> 00:07:19,227
something.

185
00:07:19,830 --> 00:07:21,629
And therefore we need this more elaborate

186
00:07:21,629 --> 00:07:24,119
solution where we don't just check the input

187
00:07:24,119 --> 00:07:27,380
number but also all the results of divisions

188
00:07:27,492 --> 00:07:27,974
by 2.

189
00:07:29,838 --> 00:07:32,847
And therefore now we derived a function that

190
00:07:32,879 --> 00:07:33,458
hopefully

191
00:07:34,085 --> 00:07:35,003
gives us true,

192
00:07:35,534 --> 00:07:36,756
false, false, true,

193
00:07:37,425 --> 00:07:39,139
true, false as an output.

194
00:07:39,683 --> 00:07:40,490
Well, let's check this.

195
00:07:43,252 --> 00:07:45,325
And that is the case. True, false, false,

196
00:07:45,405 --> 00:07:47,430
true, false, as expected.

197
00:07:48,073 --> 00:07:50,242
So this is an algorithm that allows us to

198
00:07:50,242 --> 00:07:52,945
determine whether a number can be calculated

199
00:07:53,042 --> 00:07:54,560
with 2 at the power of something.

200
00:07:55,319 --> 00:07:57,564
And I hope I could make it clear why we need

201
00:07:57,564 --> 00:08:00,131
a solution like this and why just checking

202
00:08:00,244 --> 00:08:02,420
for the divisibility by 2

203
00:08:02,963 --> 00:08:03,671
is not enough.
